  "text": "Flint Animal Cancer Center Staff – Flint Animal Cancer Center\nSkip to content\ncolorado state\nuniversity\nCSU\nflint animal\ncancer center\nAbout Us\nOur Story\nFACC Team\nContact Us\nNews\nFor Owners\nOur Services\nCancer Information Request\nAppointments\nTreatment Options\nPreparing for Your Visit\nFrequently Asked Questions\nFor DVMs\nConsult Line\nTreatment Options\nOne Cure\nAbout One Cure\nRacing for One Cure\nDonate to One Cure\nClinical Trials\nAbout Clinical Trials\nCurrent Clinical Trials\nEducation & Research\nComparative Oncology Research\nOncology Specialty Training\nDonate\nGreatest Need\nPatient Assistance\nOne Cure\nScholarship\nResearch\nFeline Cancer Research\nFACC Friends\nmenu\nclose\nTag:\nFlint Animal Cancer Center Staff\nsearch\nread more\nOur Team\nVet Tech Team Brings Passion And Experience To Provide Unparalleled Care\nLauren Mingus\n|\nOctober 17, 2018\nOur veterinary technicians are critical members of the Flint Animal Cancer Center team. With up to 30 patient visits each day, they help manage a variety of responsibilities from check-in to administering treatment. While they share many of the same passions – a love of animals and finding a cure for cancer – our vet […]\nread more\nOur Team\nFlint Animal Cancer Center Focuses on Opportunities\nLauren Mingus\n|\nNovember 30, 2020\nAfter pivoting to address the crisis caused by the global pandemic last spring, the team at the Flint Animal Cancer Center is thinking of the future and reimagining what is possible for cancer research, treatment, and prevention. “Despite the pandemic, cancer hasn’t taken a break and neither has our team,” said Dr. Rodney Page, director, […]\nread more\nOur Team\nDr. Susan Lana named director of the Flint Animal Cancer Center\nKate Shelton\n|\nOctober 3, 2024\nThe Flint Animal Cancer Center (FACC) at Colorado State University’s James L. Voss Veterinary Teaching Hospital has earned a reputation as a global leader in veterinary oncology and comparative oncology. That legacy will continue with the center’s newly named director, Dr. Susan Lana. “Dr. Lana’s deep expertise as a clinician, educator, and researcher uniquely positions […]\nbrowse articles by topic\nFACC Patient Stories\nLatest News\nOne Cure Clinical Trials\nOne Cure Patients\nOur Team\nPet Cancer Treatment\nResearch\nStories of Hope\nTeaching and Learning\nbrowse articles by tag\nBone Cancer\nBrain Tumor\nCancer Research\nCancer Stories\nCanine Cancer\nCanine Cancer Clinical Trials\nCanine Cancer Prevention Vaccine\ncanine clinical trial\nCanine Hemangiosarcoma\nCanine Leg Amputation\nCanine Lymphoma\nCanine Nasal Tumor\nCanine Osteosarcoma\nCanine Soft Tissue Sarcoma canine cancer clinical trials\nCaring for pets with cancer\ncat cancer\nChemotherapy\ncomparative oncology\nComparative Oncology Research\nDan Regan\nDiagnostic Imaging\nDiet for Pets with Cancer\nEmotional Support\nfeline cancer\nFeline GI Lymphoma\nFeline Lymphoma\nFlint Animal Cancer Center Staff\nGlioma\nGolden Retriever Lifetime Study\nHemangiosarcoma\nLaiks Fund\nlimb-spare surgery\nNasal Osteosarcoma\nNews\nOne Cure\nOne Health\nPatient Assistance Funds\nPatient Care\nPatient Stories\nPatient Story\nPet Cancer\nPet Cancer Comparative Oncology\nPet Cancer Patient Assistance Funds\nPet Cancer Prevention\nPet Cancer Terms\nPet Cancer Treatment\nPet Grief Counseling\npet leg amputation\nPet Loss\nPet Quality of Life\nPlasmacytomas\nRacing for One Cure\nradiation biology\nRadiation Bolus\nRadiation Oncology Research\nRadiation Therapy\nradioimmunology\nResearch\nSoft Tissue Sarcoma\nSpeeding up the Cure\nSurgery\nVeterinary Oncology\nVeterinary Oncology History\nVeterinary Oncology Specialist Training\nVeterinary Oncology Specialty Training\nVeterinary Oncology Training\nVeterinary Radiation Oncology\nWarning Signs of Pet Cancer\nPatient Care Quicklinks\nAppointments\nOur Services\nTreatment Options\nFrequently Asked Questions\nPreparing for Your Visit\nConsult A Professional\nResources